  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **NIRC Section 51-A**: Substituted Filing of Income Tax Returns by Employees Receiving Purely Compensation Income.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51-A simplifies the filing requirements for employees who receive purely compensation income from a single employer, provided that the employer has correctly withheld the necessary income tax. This means that instead of filing a separate income tax return, these employees can rely on the withholding certificate issued by their employer as proof of tax compliance.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis provision reduces the administrative burden on employees who meet the criteria, allowing them to avoid the complexities of filing an annual income tax return. It streamlines the tax process for a significant number of workers, ensuring that those whose tax obligations are already met through withholding do not face unnecessary paperwork.",
